-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A2. Enabling Access
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Access to system tables is governed like any other table through Unity Catalog grants. This can be done through the catalog explorer user interface, or via DBSQL. For example, to provide `audit` table access to the `engg` group, execute the following command in a notebook or SQL query editor:
-- MAGIC <div class="code-block" data-language="sql">
-- MAGIC GRANT USE CATALOG ON CATALOG system TO `engg`;
-- MAGIC GRANT USE SCHEMA ON SCHEMA system.access TO `engg`;
-- MAGIC GRANT SELECT ON TABLE system.access.audit TO `engg`;
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #1976d2; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       <ul>
-- MAGIC         <li>The above three grants could be combined into a single statement granting all three privileges on the <code>system</code> catalog; however this would open up permissions on all tables in all schemas.</li>
-- MAGIC         <li>In order to manage grants on the <code>system</code> you must have metastore admin and account admin privileges.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
