-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ### B3. Classification Tags versus Governed Tags
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Databricks provides predefined system tags that support use cases like data classification and tooling that automates it. You can also create your own custom governed tags.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Both can be used in ABAC policies — you do not have to define custom governed tags if you don't need them. But, system tags are designed primarily around data classification, whereas governed tags provide tagging capabilities in a generic sense, bringing significantly more flexibility to your data governance patterns. The next section details how to properly plan and design standards for governed tags.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ### B4. Governed Tags and Standards
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Defining governed tags means creating account-level tags (with policies) that standardize allowed keys/values and who can assign them, across all workspaces and catalogs. These tags become the attributes your ABAC policies evaluate, and they inherit down the object hierarchy during policy evaluation (catalog → schema → tables; not to columns), enabling broad, consistent enforcement with minimal duplication.  
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Key outcomes and decisions to lock down include:
-- MAGIC - A governed tag taxonomy (keys and allowed values) aligned to your business, compliance, and data protection needs.
-- MAGIC - A permission model for tag creation and assignment (who can create/edit tags, who can apply them) and the review/approval flow.  
-- MAGIC - Standards for where tags are applied (catalog, schema, table, column), noting that ABAC policy evaluation inherits tags downward but not to columns.  
-- MAGIC - Naming and value conventions, validation rules, and anti-patterns (e.g., no secrets in tag text because tags are plain text and may be replicated globally).  
-- MAGIC - Guardrails and constraints: required privileges to apply tags, max counts and lengths, and disallowed characters.  
-- MAGIC - Integration points with ABAC policies and Data Classification (system classification tags and workflows).  
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC

